 "response": "Mifa's budget is now **$1825K**. I stepped through the records by hand, which is error-prone over 1,600 entries, so treat the arithmetic with some care.\n\n**Which records counted**\n- Only Finance Office budget entries change the budget. Messages from Sales, Legal, Vendor calls and the other teams were ignored, as were non-budget Finance notes such as audits, receipts and purchase orders.\n- The budget starts from #0001, which set it to $1040K. Every other effective Finance Office increase or decrease was then applied once, in order.\n\n**How withdrawals were handled**\nFor each chain of withdrawals, I worked back from the last withdrawal, which nothing later cancels. A withdrawn update counts as never having happened, so each link flips the status of the one before it. For example:\n- **#0756** (+$521K) is excluded because #1367 withdraws it.\n- **#0009** (+$464K) is excluded through the chain #0818 \u2192 #0454 \u2192 #0117 \u2192 #0076 \u2192 #0071 \u2192 #0063 \u2192 #0016 \u2192 #0009. Following that chain, #0016's withdrawal of #0009 ends up standing.\n- **#0005** (+$543K) is restored. #0599 withdraws #0040, so #0040's withdrawal of #0005 no longer counts.\n- **#0151** (\u2212$203K) is restored through #1493 \u2192 #1462 \u2192 #0401 \u2192 #0261.\n- **#0058** (+$227K) is restored through #1115 \u2192 #0141 \u2192 #0112 \u2192 #0068.\n- **#0372** (+$531K) is restored through #0733 \u2192 #0538 \u2192 #0439 \u2192 #0410.\n\nANSWER: $1825K",
